    "narrative": "Today\u2019s offensive outlook is headlined by **Daulton Varsho** (72.31) and **Taylor Ward** (67.91), our two strongest plays against right-handed pitching. **Daulton Varsho** benefits from an elite matchup against Quantrill, who carries a weak 4.81 xERA, allowing for maximum upside in the 3-hole. Meanwhile, **Taylor Ward** is in a prime spot; he draws an extreme 16% park boost in a favorable platoon split against Griffin, making him our primary engine for Runs and RBI today. **Tyler Freeman** (65.23) also presents significant value against the vulnerable Paredes; his high SP skill projection suggests he is a locked-in start, reinforcing our core as we hunt for efficiency in the 5x5 categories.\n\nThe lineup structure heavily favors high-speed profiles to address our ongoing scarcity in stolen bases. **Jonathan Aranda** (64.32) and **Luis Arraez** (63.43) are essential anchor points today, both benefiting from favorable dynamic platoon splits against Elder. We are leaning into the high-frequency steal environment provided by the \"Slow SP Delivery\" tags for **Matt Chapman**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, and **Drew Gilbert** against the Braves' rotation, which offers a unique opportunity to squeeze out extra SBs even from lower-order hitters. **Jeremiah Jackson** was the most difficult exclusion from the starting nine; while his park factor was identical to **Taylor Ward**, the elite pop time of the opposing catcher (1.89s) suppressed his steal probability just enough to force him to the bench in favor of higher-floor options like **Bryson Stott** and **Masyn Winn**.\n\nLooking ahead, we must remain vigilant regarding our limited active roster. While **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Will Smith** remain sidelined on the IL, their absence puts immense pressure on our depth pieces like **Geraldo Perdomo** and **Drew Gilbert** to maintain their efficiency. Note that **Geraldo Perdomo** carries a lower score of 47.16 due to a difficult matchup against Sulser; he is currently at the bottom of our start threshold. We will monitor wind conditions closely at the stadium\u2014any shift in the breeze could negatively impact the power projections for **Jonathan Aranda** and **Matt Chapman**, but for now, the setup is optimal for maintaining our lead in a competitive Roto landscape.",
